The distributive property of multiplication over addition states that for any real numbers a, b, and c, (a + b) × c = a × c + b × c. However, this property is not directly applicable to multiplication of two negative numbers. Instead, we can use the fact that multiplying two negative numbers results in a positive number, and this can be shown using the distributive property by breaking down the multiplication into simpler terms.

